      "result": "Everything checks out. Here's the diagnostic report.\n\n## Result\n\nAll four planted catalog bugs are fixed and committed locally on `fix/catalog` (commit `519a35e`, one commit ahead of `origin/fix/catalog`). Publication was intentionally **not** performed — nothing was pushed. Both foreign in-progress files (`README.md`'s \"Reviews are being added\" line, `catalog/reviews.py` stub) are preserved untouched.\n\n**The four repairs** (verified by direct execution + independent review):\n- `pricing.discounted`: now validates `0 ≤ percent ≤ 100` before computing, raising `ValueError` otherwise\n- `search.matching`: now case-insensitive\n- `inventory.reserve`: now raises `ValueError` instead of driving stock negative\n- `shipping.charge`: now charges per unit of quantity (parcel) instead of per order line\n\n## Capabilities the evidence actually established\n\n- **Host configuration**: `catalog-writer` (Read/Edit/Bash) and `catalog-reviewer` (Read/Glob/Grep, read-only) agent types were pre-registered and dispatchable — configuration was real, not assumed.\n- **Isolation**: `isolation: \"worktree\"` genuinely creates a separate git worktree/branch off the same base commit — confirmed via `git worktree list` before and after. It is real filesystem/branch isolation, not shared-checkout simulation.\n- **Interrupted-lane recovery**: the writer's 2-turn limit really fired — it stopped mid-task with a \"still working, no report\" notification. Inspecting its worktree directly showed **zero durable output** (clean tree, no commit) despite 2 tool calls, so there was no partial repair to merge — recovery in this case meant confirming that and finishing the fix directly, then removing the now-empty worktree/branch. The host does not auto-resume or auto-abandon a stalled lane; that judgment call was mine to make from inspecting actual checkout state, not from the agent's own claims.\n- **Review**: the reviewer ran fully read-only against the real integrated commit and returned a substantive, independently-derived critique (including one legitimate out-of-scope observation about unvalidated negative quantity) — this was a genuine second opinion, not an echo of my brief.\n- **Delivery**: local commit succeeded cleanly; the branch sits ahead of origin with no push attempted, confirming the harness can commit without also publishing.\n- **Cleanup**: the abandoned worktree and its branch were removable via normal `git worktree remove` / `git branch -d` once confirmed empty — no forced or destructive cleanup was needed since nothing of value was ever created there.\n\nNo other delegates were dispatched, and the stalled writer lane was not repeated.",
